After maize has been shelled and dried to a 12-13% moisture level, it must be stored in a secure granary or container. The storage must be airtight, moisture-proof, and free from holes to protect against rain, rodents, and other pests.
\par 
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 To maintain quality for food or market, store the grain in hermetic plastic bags or another type of storage that does not absorb moisture.
\par 
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 For long-term storage (more than one month), preventive pesticide treatment is recommended. Options include:
\par 
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 Treating the grain with the pesticide Actellic or Ethiolathion.
\par 
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 If pesticides are unavailable, an alternative method is to mix the maize with teff or finger millet.
\par 
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 If pests still appear despite these methods, the granary should be fumigated periodically using a pesticide confirmed as appropriate for this purpose.
